h setting up  dynamic lifestyle imaging  i will then give a brief intro to our  turnkey select platform which enables  dynamic lifestyle imaging with any  existing inverted microscopes  main part of the presentation today will  be applications demonstrating the  utility of the cellulasic system with  particular emphasis given to suspension  cells such as t lymphocytes which play  crucial role in immuno oncology  let's start with some background  information on dynamic life cell imaging  i think by now it is very well  established that lifestyle imaging  offers tremendous biological insight  over traditional static imaging due to  spatial and temporal information  for example here we are showing the  static image of t lymphocytes loaded  with a fluorescent calcium indicator dye  at this point not much inside can be  gained perhaps other than what appears  to be different level of fluorescence  among the t cells  now if we were to take time-lapse image  of these t-cells  as shown in the bottom of the slide  we start to gain deeper level of  understanding  to the spatial temporal dynamics of  these cells at single cell level  in this particular experiment t cells  were activated with ionomycin which  causes increasing intracellular calcium  level  already couple observations can be made  which were not possible but we're just  looking at the static image in the  middle of the slide  for example we can notice that t cells  are oscillating at their calcium level  during the resting stage  and also that there is a significant  level of heterogeneity among the t cells  in terms of their costly responses upon  activation  let's play the movie itself to better  appreciate what is going on  in summary the advantages of dynamic  lifestyle imaging can be summarized in  this slide  analysis cellular event at single cell  level  thus enabling study of population  heterogeneity  study of cellular biology as a function  of microenvironmental perturbations  for example we can study calcium  responses of t-cells before  during and after their activation  another common example would be dynamic  gas control such as cycling between  democracy and hypoxic conditions  last but not least is the time dimension  where we can now study various cellular  responses such as morphology movement  signaling  as well as a cell cell interaction  as a function of time to obtain spatial  temporal information of any given  biological system  now let's take a step back  and think about some of the challenges  in terms of building or buying a system  which will enable dynamic lifestyle  imaging  dynamic lifestyle imaging while it is a  very powerful tool has its challenges  this is an image from wikipedia and  nicely demonstrates the complexity of  such a system  these are very large and complex systems  with a high price tag  requiring well-trained scientists to  operate  also in all cases additional  do-it-yourself components are required  to enable perfusion and fluid  capabilities in order to create true  dynamic imaging system  these components such as pumps and  proficient chambers with associated  controllers will further create  complexity and increase price  switching gears then uh let's talk about  our celesic platform  what would be the key advantages of our  system  to start it is a true turnkey product  with integrated environmental control  system coupled to microfluidic plate  where cells will be cultured and imaged  the system controller shown in the  middle of the slide is the size of a  typical 13-inch laptop in its x and y  dimension  it is extremely portable and was built  with mobility in mind  the controller controls various  parameters such as temperature gas and  flow rate within the microfluidics plate  which is connected to the controller by  manifold  the software is very easy to use and  enables step step protocol building  where each experimental step can be  built with user-defined time temperature  gas and proficient parameter such as  flow rate  let's take a look at the plate  in greater details  it has standard 96 well footprint  image in the center show  one of our plate pre-loaded with colored  dies to show individual layout of the  fluidics  plate has a 16 knot oils on the left  side and two outlet wells on the right  side  connected to the central tissue culture  chamber area via microfluidics channel  as you can see in this cartoon for each  role indicators are group 1 2 3 and 4  all the individual well within the group  are connected to tissue culture chamber  area via individual microfluidics  channels which are the colored lines  this enables up to four independent  experiments to be conducted per plate  when the plane is connected to the  controller unit vr manifold media or  reagent in each of the inlet wells can  be pressed down via positive pressure  this will then move the media or reagent  from that well into the tissue culture  chamber area  and which will then will exit to the  outer wells  essentially this creates a system where  any desired media or reagent can be  precisely delivered to cells in the  chamber area  at desired time  for specific duration and with specific  flow rate  since the plate can be temperature and  gas control  we now have a system that can offer  ability to control cellular micro  environment in dynamic on demand fashion  plate material is also made of gas  permeable polymer to allow dynamic gas  control  and the bottom of the plate is made of  n1.5 glass for clear imaging including  confocal applications  last thing i would like to mention is  that since these are microfluidics plate  we can also introduce specific micro  dimensional features  targeting certain applications such as  imaging of suspension cells or  maintenance of chemotactic gradient  now let's go over some of the key  applications  our system can be connected to two  independent gas outlets  so in this example we can create nomoxy  and hypoxic conditions using gas  switching ability  the middle image shows fluorescent  intensity of reverse oxygen sensor rtdp  measured from one of the tissue culture  chamber within our microfluidic plate  rttp will increase fluorescence with  decreasing oxygen concentration and vice  versa  arrows indicate the time point at which  gas switching was initiated  we can see rtdp fluorescence increasing  as we put tissue chamber under hypoxic  condition  starting at t equals two hours  when we revert to no maxi condition  at t equals 6.5 hours we can see  fluorescence start to decrease  now that we have established that our  system can create hypoxic or nomoxic  microenvironment  the image on the right shows cellular  responses under such conditions by  measuring expression level of heatphone  alpha which is a key transcription  factor under cellular hypoxia  we are also measuring itdp fluorescence  as indicated by blue line  when cells are subjected to hypoxic  condition  we see the expression level of heatphone  alpha increasing as seen by the increase  in the black line  and then later on as cells are subjected  to the maxi condition we see  fluorescence of rtdp decreasing which in  turn is followed rapidly by decreased  expression of hyphen alpha  intensity of dappy is plotted as a  control in purple line  and it shows no meaningful change under  changing oxygen levels  next we would like to show you lifestyle  movie generated using biotracker hypoxia  lifestyle dye this is a cell permeable  lifestyle dye which becomes fluorescent  under hypoxic condition inside of cells  here we're looking at a431 cells  loaded with and without dye after 16  hour incubation under hypoxic condition  to show its specificity  now let's take a look at the livestream  movie  next we will look at the autophagosomes  formation under hypoxia using  fluorescent lysosomal marker lc3  under hypoxic condition  cellular stress will induce the  formation of punctate autophagosomes  and this can be visualized and measured  based on lifestyle imaging  let's take a look at the movie  next applications we're looking at  intracellular trafficking of proteins  in this case  we are examining internalization of  fluorescent egf receptor upon egf  activation you will notice upon the  addition of egf the receptors start to  collapse together which then gets  internalized to endosomal compartment  with characteristic punctate patterns  let's take a look at the lifestyle movie  while the migration and innovation  is widely performed on membrane  platforms  did not allow life cell imaging for  obvious reasons  here we now show how microfluidics  can enable live cell imaging of cellular  migration  while maintaining chemotactic gradient  we have a microfluidics culture chamber  that is connected to two parallel flow  channels  cells are cultured in the middle chamber  and chemoattractant is perfused into an  adjacent channel  as you can see in the images at the  bottom  cells will migrate towards the presence  of chemoattractant  let's take a look  perhaps most obvious utility of dynamic  lifestyle imaging is calcium imaging  many cell types respond to external  stimulation by increasing intracellular  calcium level often these calcium  responses are transient responses which  only last for short duration of time  bottom images of the slide show calcium  responses of hela cells to atp  and you can see that the response occurs  within a minute of atp introduction  imaging this type of rapid transient  responses require on-demand dynamic  imaging capability  now let's take a closer look at the atp  induced calcium responses  of healer cells  we will cover one more example of  calcium imaging where cells are  undergoing rapid spontaneous calcium  oscillation  emission the rise shows  cardiac muscle cells undergoing a  spontaneous contraction  with life cell imaging we can better  understand the temporal dynamics of such  behavior  images on the left show calcium  fluctuation of individual cells over  time  we can see that the cells are actually  beating every two to three seconds as  seen by the ups and downs of the calcium  level let's take a closer look at the  livestream movie  next i would like to cover lifestyle  imaging of suspension cells  which pose unique challenge due to their  non-other hearing nature  as you can see on the image at the  bottom left  during life cell imaging suspension  cells will move up and down making it  impossible to image cells at single cell  level  however if we introduce micro scale  ceiling then we can confine the cells  under single focal plane and enable  clear visualization of cells during life  cell imaging  now we can use this micro sealing  feature  to examine in great detail cell cell  interaction of t cells with that of  antigen presenting b cells  let's take a closer look  here's another example where we're  examining t cell appetizers at single  cell level  we're using cd95 activation to induce  programmed cell death and then  visualizing the cellular events using  caspase-3 specific apoptosis probe as  well as annexing 5. let's take a look at  the livestream movie  i would like to close the application  part with 3d live cell imaging  we know that currently 3d tissue  culturing is very hot topic  shown on the left side are images of mcf  cells  grown in our microfluidic plate compared  to a regular chamber slide  let's take a closer look at how these  cells form 3d structures in our plate  in closing out  i would like to mention some additional  features of our system  in addition to dynamic lifestyle imaging  it can be used as an automation platform  for tasks such as staining  we can also enable extraction of cells  after imaging for example trypsinite  cells can be interrogated by flow  cytometry  proteins or nucleic acid can also be  collected and analyzed as  well that covers our applications  overview  now for summary i would like to quickly  go over our plate offerings  we have number plates targeted for  different cell types  so all our plates that start with letter  m are intended for mammalian imaging  whereas our plates with letter b and y  are intended for bacteria and east  imaging respectively  we do enjoy a tremendous number of  publications many of them in top  journals further demonstrating the value  that we bring for our customers  now in summary  we know that the real in vivo biology is  complex and dynamic  an ability to perform dynamic life cell  imaging  offers unique window of opportunity to  better understand these events  with celasic we can now better control  the dynamic cellular micro environment  with turnkey offering leveraging  microfluidics  our system enables wide range of studies  which can better recapitulate complex  individual biology  with that i would like to thank everyone  if you have any questions please do not  hesitate to contact us or visit us at  www.cell  thank you  you

